  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Resilience of Communities through Mine Clearance and the Improvement of the Agricultural Infrastructure (Project RECLAIM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe&#x2019;s National Development Strategy (NDS-1) emphasizes inclusive development, yet communities along the borders with Mozambique and South Africa remain affected by landmine contamination from the liberation struggle. Despite progress, around 12 square kilometres of explosive ordinance remain, hindering access to agricultural land and basic services, and posing ongoing risks to lives and livelihoods. Zimbabwe, bound by the Ottawa Convention, aims to be mine-free by 2030 following a five-year</narrative>
  </description>
